BT 1 0 0 1 0 47.5 Tm /F1 9 Tf 11.3 TL (Does participating in global supply chains help firms innovate? The authors use enterprise surveys from 144 economies, with most) Tj T* (observations in low- and middle-income countries. They compare firms before and after entry into two-way trade and check results) Tj T* (against matched comparisons. Product innovation rises more consistently than process innovation, and imported inputs appear to) Tj T* (account for much of the gain. Lower-income economies show stronger foreign-technology adoption. Trade entry is not randomized,) Tj T* (so firms' plans to innovate could influence when they start trading.) Tj T* ET
